Q: Painting order with single-area grid A: <p>Make the div explicitly behind</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>outer {
  display: grid;
  grid-template-areas: "singlearea";
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  isolation: isolate; /* you may need this if the div disappear behind something else */

  &gt;* {
    grid-area: singlearea;
  }
}

div {
  opacity: .33;
  z-index: -1; /* Added */
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-html lang-html prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;outer&gt;
  &lt;div&gt;
    &lt;svg viewBox="0 0 2 1"&gt;&lt;rect fill="red" width="2" height="1"/&gt;&lt;/svg&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;hgroup&gt;
    &lt;h1&gt;and so on&lt;/h1&gt;
  &lt;/hgroup&gt;
&lt;/outer&gt;</code></pre>
</div>
</div>
</p>

Q: How to use cv::Mat imgbuf created by pointer to video data A: <p>Test this method:</p>

<pre><code>unsigned char *mem = (unsigned char*)mmap(NULL, page_offset + len,
 PROT_READ |PROT_WRITE, MAP_PRIVATE, fd, page_base); 

cv::Mat imgbuf(480,640, CV_8UC3, &amp;mem[0]);
cv::Mat img_2, img_3;
cv::resize(imgbuf,img_2,cv::Size(640,480));
img_2.copyTo(img_3);
auto result = v-&gt;facedetection(img_2);

for (const auto &amp;r : result.rects)
{
   cv::Rect myR = cv::Rect(r.x * img_2.cols, r.y * img_2.rows, (int)(r.width * img_2.cols), 
   (int)(r.height * img_2.rows));

   cv::rectangle(img_3,myR,Scalar(0, 0, 255), 1);
}
imshow("Result", img_3);
waitKey(0);
</code></pre>

<p>After getting a valid result you can optimize this and use less of "Mat"s.</p>

Q: How do I make the menu button open the nav menu in media queries A: <p>I have added a <code>nav</code> with the id of <code>sidebar</code> to a snippet I copied from yours and the toggle works. Hence you seemingly don't have a <code>nav</code> with the <code>id</code> of <code>sidebar</code> (yet?) when your <code>sidebar</code> variable is initialized, or, alternatively, your screen may have a greater <code>width</code> than 800 when you test.</p>
<p><div class="snippet" data-lang="js" data-hide="false" data-console="true" data-babel="false" data-babel-preset-react="false" data-babel-preset-ts="false">
<div class="snippet-code">
<pre class="snippet-code-js lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>// app.js

const sidebar = document.getElementById('sidebar')

function toggleSidebar() {
  sidebar.classList.toggle('show')
}</code></pre>
<pre class="snippet-code-css lang-css prettyprint-override"><code>/* Media queries for responsiveness */

@media screen and (max-width: 800px) {

  body {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    grid-template-areas:
      "logo"
      "sidebar"
      "main"
      "footer";
  }

  nav {
    position: fixed;
    width: 300px;
    display: none;
  }

  .show {
    display: block;
  }

}

.icon {
  width: 16px;
  height: auto;
}</code></pre>
